      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Zephyr ITE support does expose an API to clear pending interrupts, and we use it [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/tasks.c;l\u003d441).\n\nIt looks like it might also be required to call `it8xxx2_wuc_clear_status()` for GPIOs specifically.  But lookup of the correct WUC device based on the GPIO needs some research.\n\nHowever, I don\u0027t see any Zephyr boards enabling CEC.  I recommend stubbing out `gpio_clear_pending_interrupt()` in the Zephyr GPIO shim and adding a TODO bug.",
